    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "dTtTmgzHSTX5"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 9. Clinical baselines: ASA, NELA, POSSUM, NEWS2\n",
        "*(research doc §2.4 — \"ASA, POSSUM, NELA, all differences clearly laid out\")*\n",
        "\n",
        "None of these four are machine-learned — they're fixed equations (or, for ASA, a\n",
        "clinical judgement) developed once on external cohorts, included here specifically as the\n",
        "non-learning baselines any model in this project has to beat. `nela.py` already\n",
        "implements NELA. `score_models.py` already implements NEWS2 but it isn't compared to\n",
        "anything elsewhere in the repo. **POSSUM was the one of the four not yet implemented\n",
        "anywhere in this codebase — added below**, following the standard published equation\n",
        "(Copeland et al. 1991; Portsmouth correction: Prytherch et al. 1998).\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 21,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "FaEYML_tSTX5",
        "outputId": "86a919a3-700c-436a-b3bd-a7279f47f6ac"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "NELA demo risk (illustrative inputs): 0.1770\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "import nela\n",
        "import score_models\n",
        "\n",
        "# --- NELA demo, using the repo's own worked example patient, 100033460 -----------------\n",
        "# NELA needs several \"centred\" variables (deviation from the NELA derivation cohort's own\n",
        "# mean, e.g. Age_cent = age - population_mean_age) that INSPIRE doesn't give us directly --\n",
        "# research doc §2.4 flags this as a real external-validation question, not just a coding\n",
        "# detail. This call demonstrates the mechanism with illustrative values, exactly as the\n",
        "# `if __name__ == \"__main__\"` block at the bottom of nela.py does.\n",
        "demo_risk = nela.compute_nela_score(\n",
        "    Age_cent=5, ASA_3=1, Albumin=35,\n",
        "    Pulse_cent=10, Pulse_cent2=100,\n",
        "    SystolicBP_cent=-5, SystolicBP_cent2=25,\n",
        "    LN_Urea_cent=0.3, LN_WBC_cent=0.2, LN_WBC_cent2=0.04,\n",
        "    GCS_14=1, Malignancy_Primary=1, Respiratory_2=1,\n",
        "    Urgency_2_6=1, Indication_Sepsis=1, Soiling_Severe=1,\n",
        ")\n",
        "print(f\"NELA demo risk (illustrative inputs): {demo_risk:.4f}\")\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 22,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "R9uV9PEKSTX5",
        "outputId": "5433625c-6d08-4a65-839f-cbbd61ff7623"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "POSSUM   demo risk (PS=20, OS=16): 0.1324\n",
            "P-POSSUM demo risk (PS=20, OS=16): 0.0391\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "def compute_possum_score(physiological_score, operative_severity_score, variant='possum'):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    POSSUM / P-POSSUM mortality risk.\n",
        "\n",
        "    physiological_score, operative_severity_score: sum of 12 (physiology) and 6\n",
        "        (operative) POSSUM sub-scores, each individually scored 1/2/4/8 by severity.\n",
        "        This notebook does not derive those sub-scores from INSPIRE fields (that mapping\n",
        "        is itself a research task -- see docs/research_questions_and_roadmap.md §2.4) --\n",
        "        pass them in directly, e.g. from a manual chart review or once a mapping exists.\n",
        "    variant: 'possum' (original, Copeland et al. 1991) or 'p-possum'\n",
        "        (Portsmouth correction, Prytherch et al. 1998 -- corrects POSSUM's tendency to\n",
        "        overestimate mortality in low-risk patients).\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    import math\n",
        "    ps, os_ = physiological_score, operative_severity_score\n",
        "    if variant == 'possum':\n",
        "        logit = -7.04 + 0.13 * ps + 0.16 * os_          # R1 = mortality risk (Copeland et al.)\n",
        "    elif variant == 'p-possum':\n",
        "        logit = -9.065 + 0.1692 * ps + 0.155 * os_      # Portsmouth correction\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        raise ValueError(\"variant must be 'possum' or 'p-possum'\")\n",
        "    return 1 / (1 + math.exp(-logit))\n",
        "\n",
        "# Demo, using the same illustrative severity level as the NELA example above:\n",
        "print(f\"POSSUM   demo risk (PS=20, OS=16): {compute_possum_score(20, 16, 'possum'):.4f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"P-POSSUM demo risk (PS=20, OS=16): {compute_possum_score(20, 16, 'p-possum'):.4f}\")\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 23,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "O86zfRnZSTX5",
        "outputId": "c17b504d-5956-4274-e817-23308c402591"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "NEWS2 demo score: 7\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# NEWS2 demo -- score_models.py already has this, unused elsewhere in the repo.\n",
        "# It's a vitals-only, deterioration-focused score (built for ward monitoring), a genuinely\n",
        "# different kind of tool from the pre-op-risk-focused ASA/POSSUM/NELA above -- worth\n",
        "# deciding whether it belongs in the same comparison table or a separate one.\n",
        "news2_demo = score_models.compute_news2_score(\n",
        "    resp_rate=22, spo2=94, temp=38.2, systolic_bp=105,\n",
        "    heart_rate=115, consciousness='A', oxygen_support=False,\n",
        ")\n",
        "print(f\"NEWS2 demo score: {news2_demo}\")\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "_lfGo4nsSTX5"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 10. GBM baseline (Model 2)\n",
        "*(`docs/INSPIRE_Project_Notes.md` §3 — \"Saranya's model\")*\n",
        "\n",
        "Builds the same 18-feature pre-op snapshot table `gbm_mortality_pipeline.py` builds\n",
        "(demographics + most-recent pre-op labs), reusing the `subjects` already loaded above\n",
        "instead of re-reading from disk. Fits a plain Logistic Regression, the same baseline\n",
        "comparator the original script uses (full XGBoost needs more data than this 30-patient\n",
        "subset can support meaningfully — swap `LogisticRegression` for\n",
        "`xgboost.XGBClassifier` once running at full scale, exactly as `docs/INSPIRE_Project_Notes.md`\n",
        "§3 describes).\n"
      ]
    },
